WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.140
I must say, I'm shocked.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.490
A dragon, you say?

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.120
A dragon-shaped light was observed 
by witnesses, that is all.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.750
What concerns me is rather this "humanoid 
something" which was fighting it.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.000
What do you believe it was?

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.420
A Peacemaker.

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.000
Admittedly, that is purely 
my personal opinion.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:00.440
I thought that you were a realist 
through and through, Major Sturm.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:04.720
Whatever it was, Shannon Cassul defeated it.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.690
This fact cannot be overlooked.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.760
If we leave it be,

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.270
people will come forward to attempt 
to claim this power. Already, the...

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:17.700
Third Princess of the Giat 
Empire, Senes Lur Giat...

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.450
That crisis management organization 
she runs... "Scarlet," is it?

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:24.330
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.750
Scarlet has been exhibiting odd behavior,

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.710
especially these past two years.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.250
A rebellion?

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.090
It is possible.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.340
The Scrapped Princess and 
her party possess power

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.680
capable of destroying this world's 
balance of power in one stroke.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.410
You have a point.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.140
Thank you, Major Sturm.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.570
"Waltz of the Abandoned Dog of a Girl"

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:09.620
Say, why do you suppose that guy

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.960
who turned into that monster 
didn't attack me directly?

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.960
He did the same thing back in Taurus.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.930
If he was going to attack me, he 
should have just come straight at me.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.400
Pacifica...

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.230
What happened? An attack?

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:34.440
No.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.520
No way!

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.690
Why did it have to pick <i>here </i>of all places?

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.950
There's nothing we could have done.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.200
Anyway, we...

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.500
We might have gone by cart 
for as far as we could go.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.290
Our traveling money is almost depleted, too.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.960
It might be time to do some thinking.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.390
Don't break it!

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:09.890
I guess nobody lives here.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.480
This way, we'll have a roof over our heads.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.350
Looks like we'll be 
stopping here for a while.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.280
Then we'll let you get to it, okay, Shannon?

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.070
You're gonna go shopping, right?

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.530
Let's see...

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.490
Salted fish and long onions.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:33.500
Potatoes, eggs... Two pairs of underwear.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.940
I think I have everything.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.300
Still, what kind of way is this for 
a kid sister to treat her brother?

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.430
See you, kid.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.500
Now look here...

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.550
This is making me look stupid.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.640
I Cin.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.510
Really? Cin, huh?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.140
Listen, Cin. I'm on a trip right now.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.300
You can't come with me.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.520
Understand?

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:43.060
Bye, now.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.130
Shannon's coming back. But he...

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.050
Tell me, Raquel...

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.560
Why is it that you can use magic?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.520
Well, I'm not really sure.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.980
You use it without knowing how?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.320
Magic is more about "feel" than thought,

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.310
so it's hard to explain in words.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.710
But Mother told me that 
its strength is determined

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.580
by the capacity of a person's awareness.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:34.740
Capacity?

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.790
That said, it doesn't mean that 
you can do anything at all

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.420
just because your capacity is great.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.830
Really?

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:41.920
Of course.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.710
Because in the end, spells 
are triggered by manipulating

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.880
the natural forces in a given location.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:52.800
He's back!

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.020
I... I'm back.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.700
You wished to see me, Baroness?

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.210
You're so formal.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.710
Why don't you call me Mother?

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:26.710
Well, I'll leave the joking at 
that and get right to the point.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.510
I want you to go to the holy city of Grendel.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:34.390
It is regarding the 5,111th 
Revelation of Grendel, yes?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.720
I'm so glad that you catch on quickly.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.020
I understand. I'll be off at once, then.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.730
Oh, that reminds me. This came for you.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.860
The sender is one Winia Chester.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.650
Winia?

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.450
Oh.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:59.200
I was so moved that you were 
getting letters from women, Chris,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:03.120
that I made a circular notice of it 
and sent copies throughout the unit.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.460
B-Baroness?!

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.100
I'm shocked!

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.420
My Christopher has an 
older woman as his lover?

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:11.960
Well?!

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:13.880
Oh, now I understand.

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:18.350
It was a purely platonic thank-you letter,

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.320
but between the lines,

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:23.390
I could see hints of the 
feelings of a young girl.

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.480
I'm amazed that you can 
read so much into things.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.230
For a lady with too much 
free time on her hands,

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:32.990
the love affairs of another 
are the ultimate pastime.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.860
Please don't say such things, ma'am.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:36.110
Are we clear?

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.910
Your destination is the holy city of Grendel.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:43.160
I don't want you wandering off and 
visiting little Winia by mistake.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.080
I won't go there.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:49.750
What are we gonna do with this girl?

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.800
That's a good question.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:56.090
But we don't know for certain 
that this girl is an orphan,

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:58.760
so if we're not careful, 
this might be a crime.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.310
And given our situation...

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.640
I know.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:05.110
I know that, but...

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:11.070
But when she looks at me with 
those eyes, I can't say no.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:15.570
This is pathetic!

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:18.780
You have to spell things out for her!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.450
We can't take her with us, and you know it!

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.910
When did you turn so heartless?

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:29.140
It's just because you brought 
a girl back with you, Shannon.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.050
I'm always heartless!

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:32.630
Oh, really?

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.210
Yes, I really am!

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.600
Um, Cin?

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:50.480
The thing is, you can't stay with us.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:51.230
Understand?

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.740
In other words, you have to say goodbye.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.200
Cin!

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.450
Oh, dear. I don't think she likes you.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.790
Don't laugh! You try talking to her, Raquel.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:07.660
I suppose you're right.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.170
Listen, Cin...

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.640
What would you like to do, Cin?

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.260
Do you have a home, Cin?

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:27.060
No.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:31.560
Oh. Then, you don't have a daddy or a mommy?

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:33.520
No.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:35.570
Did you get separated from them?

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.900
Then, have they passed away?

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.490
Wait, could it be that you 
don't remember anything?

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.040
For the time being,

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.960
let's let her spend the night here.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.960
We can't toss her out into a night like this.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:24.620
What's the matter?

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.250
Nothing!

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:35.810
So, what are we gonna do?

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:37.630
This is awkward...

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.480
Even if we forced Cin to go back to town,

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:41.930
with things the way they are, she...

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.590
Well, yeah, but still...

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:48.220
Well, we'd planned to stay here 
for at least four or five days,

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.560
so why don't we lend Shannon to Cin?

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.060
What's that supposed to mean?

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.940
What are you two mumbling about?

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:56.820
Nothing.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.250
Cin, you've been clinging 
to him this whole time.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.470
What's so great about him?

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.280
I waiting.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.580
I waiting.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.380
Shannon come.

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:09.540
So I like him.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.250
I don't understand what you mean.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:12.700
I like him.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.580
Okay, okay, I get it.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.570
It sounds like she was waiting for someone,

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.710
so I guess she mistook me for that person.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:21.400
If that's the case,

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.470
shouldn't she be waiting 
there for that person?

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:30.850
Still, I wonder if no one ever spoke 
to her until you did, Shannon?

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:33.390
It's all pretty strange.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:35.900
Anyway, once the road is dry,

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:39.190
I'll go into that town again and ask around.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.070
I guess that's all we can do for now.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.250
Cardinal Garnest Hogue?

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:04.590
My name is Christopher Bairach.

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:08.550
Bairach? The son of the Baroness?

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:12.520
Thank you for granting me an audience.

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:17.270
There are questions that 
I would like to ask you,

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:20.730
a man who is both the Cardinal 
of the Church of Mauser,

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.490
as well as the Commissioner of the 
elimination squad, the Purgers.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:26.450
Please forgive my rude manner of speaking.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.620
My original specialty was 
smashing and destroying.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.280
You're a Special Forces combat specialist?

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:36.540
Yes, and I've taken part in two operations 
to assassinate the Scrapped Princess, as well.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:44.670
Would you tell me the truth behind 
the 5,111th Revelation of Grendel?

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:46.910
The truth?

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:49.550
I'm not sure what you're getting at.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:54.680
There isn't a single document remaining 
that deals directly with that revelation.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:55.600
And what's more,

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.270
the revelations have been wrong 
as much as twice to date.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.230
Only twice.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.400
Twice too many.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.690
Does an omnipotent god make a mistake twice?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:10.530
It's possible the priests who interpreted 
the divine words were mistaken.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:14.980
The speech in the revelations is 
not the same as our words, you see.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.250
I have met the Scrapped Princess.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:22.280
As well as her brother and sister, 
whom you call the Guardians.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.050
However, no matter how hard I tried,

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.610
I could not picture her as an evil entity.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:30.390
What are you implying?

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.680
This God who tried to wipe 
out the Scrapped Princess

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.140
along with the entire town of Taurus...

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.140
What exactly is he?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:40.600
As I recall, that operation was under 
the jurisdiction of the Purgers.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:46.530
Was it really God that did that?

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:48.980
As to that, I...

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.910
Well, let's leave it at that for today.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.900
I may come to speak to you again,

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:58.580
so I look forward to your cooperation then.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.170
What's the matter?

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:21.140
You look exhausted.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.400
L-Lady Steyr!

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.650
What brings you here this day?

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.530
I'm going out for a while.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:36.700
Finding people was Galil's 
role, but he got himself killed

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.870
without handing over the job.

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:44.790
Y-You mean to say that he has passed away?!

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.640
Which means that I'll be leaving 
you here alone for a while,

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.610
so keep an eye on things, all right?

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:53.090
It can't be...

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:58.560
How could Galil, a servant of God, perish?

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.020
Enter.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.060
Excuse me.

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:20.450
Do you believe that God must be 
an all-powerful, absolute being?

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:26.420
If God is not an immortal being, then...

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.970
That isn't possible.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.880
God doesn't die because he is God,

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.310
and he is God because he can't die.

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:35.510
It is because he is just that God cannot die.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:38.790
And even if it should look that way to us,

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.560
it is because God wills it so.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.540
Seen from the end result,

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:46.480
God always points us in the right direction.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.900
God cannot die.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.480
I suppose you're right.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.030
I'll leave you to your tea, then.

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:03.040
This tastes terrible...

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:15.470
Shannon, don't work us delicate 
maidens too hard, okay?

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:17.220
Sheesh...

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:20.630
Good work.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:22.550
Sorry about that.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.140
Thanks.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.440
You're a good girl, Cin.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.100
"You're a good girl..."

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:31.770
Here you go.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.530
Careful, now. Don't spill the stuffing, okay?

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.130
You hold it like this when you eat it.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.500
Is something wrong?

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:45.960
Not really.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.200
Well, if you say so.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.420
It's strange, isn't it?

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.790
It's like our family has increased by one.

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:05.310
Hold it!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.770
What do you think you're doing?!

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.770
I go into bath.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:12.900
Shannon's in there right now!

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:14.530
I take bath with Shannon.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:18.070
Look, we'll say you're a girl 
for the sake of argument...

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:20.530
You take bath, too, Pacifica?

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:22.240
Why would I do that?

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.950
Cin like Shannon.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:27.790
Pacifica like Shannon, too?

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.540
Yeah, because Shannon is my brother.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:33.540
You like?

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:36.420
Well, I don't hate him...

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:42.140
Shannon.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.430
You have another one of those cords, right?

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.100
C'mon, now! Hold still!

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:52.230
Do you itch anywhere else?

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:53.310
No.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.520
I'm gonna rinse you off, then.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:55.450
Okay.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:03.810
Seven.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.080
Six. Seven.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:08.930
I get out.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.910
Okay, you can go.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:15.460
No running!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.540
I guess she's not such a bad kid...

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:31.390
Raquel, the bath's free.

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:35.320
Look at this! It's the 
same hairstyle as Shannon!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.990
I'm gonna make something fancy for once,

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.450
so look forward to it!

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.030
Cin help!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.080
Oh, you'll help me?

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:51.040
She's a cut above a certain 
tomboy I could mention!

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:52.830
What're you making?

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.450
It's a secret.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:56.170
Don't use any magic.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:15.810
Geez, you surprised me!

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.180
"Zefiris," right?

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:20.290
What's the matter?

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:22.770
You do not fear me.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.530
Well, we're on the same side, right?

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.860
I am what your kind calls a demon.

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:32.540
A being with vast powers of destruction.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:37.090
Maybe, but you don't use them on us, right?

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.500
So I don't think there's 
anything to be frightened of.

00:20:41.810 --> 00:20:44.510
This is sudden, but I 
require your assistance.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.260
Assistance?

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:51.570
What's this for?

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:55.140
The young girl who is with you.

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:57.940
Cin? What about her?

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:00.440
Kill that girl.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:34.340 --> 00:22:37.370
Pacifica is told by Zefiris to kill Cin.

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:41.920
There's just no telling when a person will 
suddenly be the target of another's ill will.

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:45.540
Shannon and Pacifica have a fight over Cin.

00:22:45.540 --> 00:22:47.440
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:47.440 --> 00:22:49.240
"Nocturne of Bonds and Prayers."

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
